---
// Procedurally-rendered "supply chain" motif (warehouse racks, a moving
// conveyor with packages, pulsing distribution nodes) as an actual looping
// background video, dimmed behind the Hero content. The blur is baked into
// the video's pixels at generation time (see scripts/ for the generator) —
// deliberately NOT a runtime CSS `filter: blur()`, which would force the
// browser to re-blur every decoded frame of a playing video and was
// measurably hurting paint/render performance. Purely decorative
// (aria-hidden). Respects prefers-reduced-motion by pausing playback (see
// main.ts) — the poster frame keeps the visual either way.
---

<div class="supply-chain-backdrop pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 overflow-hidden" aria-hidden="true">
  <video
    class="supply-chain-video h-full w-full object-cover"
    autoplay
    muted
    loop
    playsinline
    preload="auto"
    poster="/videos/supply-chain-poster.jpg"
    fetchpriority="high"
  >
    <source src="/videos/supply-chain-bg.webm" type="video/webm" />
    <source src="/videos/supply-chain-bg.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
  </video>

  <!-- Gradient overlay: only darkened enough behind the text column for
       legibility — the rest stays clear so the video is actually visible. -->
  <div
    class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-navy/90 via-navy/25 to-transparent dark:from-navy-deep/90 dark:via-navy-deep/30 dark:to-transparent"
  >
  </div>
  <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-navy/30 dark:from-navy-deep/35 via-transparent to-transparent"></div>
</div>
